{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011mUdqaU8specS7yspcCtEC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tslug: pose-validate-index-reads-residuals\n3\tstatus: in-progress        # draft | in-progress | done | superseded | abandoned; blocked = operational wait, not terminal\n4\tcreated_at: 2026-11-27\n5\tcompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\n6\tsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\n7\tdepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\n8\tremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\n9\tpriority: 2\n10\tcomponents: pose-mcp\n11\ttask_type: bugfix\n12\tsurface: standard\n13\tdelivers: capability:validate-index-reads-residuals\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t# Spec: pose-validate-index-reads-residuals\n17\t\n18\t## 1. Intent\n19\t\n20\t### Goal\n21\tClose what `pose-validate-read-only-index-followups` left open: changed specs of a POSE root below the repository top, the report's path redaction and UTF-8 cuts, a silent ls-files failure, and the guards still without a failing test.\n22\t\n23\t### Business value\n24\tThe spec closed on 2026-11-27 with follow-ups in its Final Report (review rounds 1–3) and its approving attestation (round 5, N1–N5). One is medium: with the POSE root below the repository top, a modified spec's ready transition goes unchecked without a finding.\n25\t\n26\t### Constraints\n27\tEach item keeps the behaviour its origin spec delivered; a fix that changes an answer states it as a decision.\n28\t\n29\t### Non-goals\n30\tReopening the decisions of the origin spec.\n31\t\n32\t## 2. Requirements\n33\t\n34\t### Functional\n35\t- R1: With the POSE root below the repository top, the ready-transition read shall list changed specs (Git names them top-relative), so their ready transitions are checked (round 1 N11, round 5 N3).\n36\t- R2: The report's redaction shall replace a whole absolute path, also one with spaces, quotes, parentheses or a leading `:`, backtick or `[` (round 5, N1).\n37\t- R3: The bounds on Git's message and the report note shall cut at a character, never inside a UTF-8 sequence (round 5, N4).\n38\t- R4: A failing `ls-files` in worktree scope selection shall fail the selection with its cause instead of silently dropping untracked files (round 5, N5).\n39\t- R5: The guards listed by rounds 2–5 shall each have a failing test: restoring `--path-format`, the `X^-` cut, the report note bound and stderr warning, `GitEnglish` on the check, lookup and hand-over, the memfd write fallback, the private copy keeping the index's time, a stand-in Git that echoes an unknown `--path-format`, and a locale test independent of installed translations; the ledger's context is L1 (rounds 1 N6–N7, 2 N16, 3 N21, 5 N2).\n40\t\n41\t### Non-functional\n42\tExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n43\t\n44\t### Security\n45\tNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n46\t\n47\t### Compatibility\n48\tRecords and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n49\t\n50\t## 3. Technical Plan\n51\t\n52\t### Affected areas\n53\t`pose-mcp`: `check.go` (ready transitions), `report.go`, `validate_scope.go`, `git_worktree_reads*.go` and their tests.\n54\t\n55\t### Artifacts\n56\t- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-validate-index-reads-residuals.md\n57\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n58\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n59\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n60\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n61\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\n62\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_reads_residuals_test.go\n63\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_index_residuals_test.go\n64\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux_test.go\n65\t\n66\t### Delivery targets\n67\t- capability:validate-index-reads-residuals module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\n68\t\n69\t### Accepted limits\n70\t- L1: The review history ledger passing its own deadline to the index lookup has no failing test. Accepted because observing it needs a stand-in Git that outlasts the ledger's 30 s deadline, and the lookup is bounded by its own 30 s otherwise, so a regression changes the bound, not the outcome.\n71\t\n72\t### API/contract changes\n73\t`pose validate` scope selection fails with its cause when the untracked listing fails, where it used to narrow silently. The report note replaces whole known directories before other absolute paths.\n74\t\n75\t### Data/storage changes\n76\tNone.\n77\t\n78\t### Technical risks\n79\tA scope selection that used to pass with a failing `ls-files` now fails; that failure was silent narrowing before.\n80\t\n81\t## 4. Tasks\n82\t\n83\t### Planning\n84\t- [x] Confirm each requirement against the current engine before starting.\n85\t\n86\t### Implementation\n87\t- [x] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n88\t\n89\t### Validation\n90\t- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n91\t\n92\t## 5. Decisions\n93\t\n94\t## 6. Validation\n95\t\n96\t### Strategy\n97\tEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n98\t\n99\t### Deterministic checks\n100\t\n101\t#### Test\n102\t- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n103\t\n104\t### Execution log\n105\t- 2026-11-27: R1 adds `--relative` to the ready-transition diff; R2 replaces the root, repository top, Git directories, temporary and home directories whole before the generic pattern, which now also starts after `:`, a backtick or `[`; R3 cuts at a character (`TruncateUTF8`); R4 fails scope selection on a failed untracked listing; R5 adds stand-in Git tests. Each guard fails its test mutated out: `TestReadyTransitionsSeeSpecsBelowTheRepositoryTop`, `TestTheReportRemovesWholePaths`, `TestBoundsCutAtACharacter`, `TestScopeSelectionReportsAFailedUntrackedListing`, `TestTheIndexLookupNeedsNoPathFormat`, `TestIndexReadsRunGitInEnglish`, `TestTheIndexFallbacksKeepTheAnswer`, `TestTheRemainingIndexReadGuards`.\n106\t\n107\t### Results summary\n108\tThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n109\t\n110\t### Requirement trace\n111\t- R1 [satisfied] test:TestReadyTransitionsSeeSpecsBelowTheRepositoryTop\n112\t- R2 [satisfied] test:TestTheReportRemovesWholePaths\n113\t- R3 [satisfied] test:TestBoundsCutAtACharacter\n114\t- R4 [satisfied] test:TestScopeSelectionReportsAFailedUntrackedListing\n115\t- R5 [satisfied] test:TestTheIndexLookupNeedsNoPathFormat, test:TestIndexReadsRunGitInEnglish, test:TestTheIndexFallbacksKeepTheAnswer, test:TestTheRemainingIndexReadGuards\n116\t\n117\t### Known gaps\n118\tNone.\n119\t\n120\t## 7. Final Report\n121\t\n122\t### Delivered scope\n123\tReady transitions see specs below the repository top; the report removes whole paths and cuts at characters; a failed untracked listing fails scope selection; every index-read guard but the ledger's deadline has a failing test.\n124\t\n125\t### Files and modules changed\n126\t`pose-mcp` check, report, validate scope and the read-only index reads, with their tests.\n127\t\n128\t### Validation executed\n129\t`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n130\t\n131\t### Residual risks\n132\tL1 above.\n133\t\n134\t### Follow-ups\n135\tNone. Origin: `pose-validate-read-only-index-followups` (done 2026-11-27).\n136\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"a628c632-6b28-474a-9dcb-5a5f674a3e68","timestamp":"2026-11-27T15:45:40.642Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-a21e9a05af/worktree/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-validate-index-reads-residuals.md","content":"---\nslug: pose-validate-index-reads-residuals\nstatus: in-progress        # draft | in-progress | done | superseded | abandoned; blocked = operational wait, not terminal\ncreated_at: 2026-11-27\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\nremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\npriority: 2\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface: standard\ndelivers: capability:validate-index-reads-residuals\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-validate-index-reads-residuals\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nClose what `pose-validate-read-only-index-followups` left open: changed specs of a POSE root below the repository top, the report's path redaction and UTF-8 cuts, a silent ls-files failure, and the guards still without a failing test.\n\n### Business value\nThe spec closed on 2026-11-27 with follow-ups in its Final Report (review rounds 1–3) and its approving attestation (round 5, N1–N5). One is medium: with the POSE root below the repository top, a modified spec's ready transition goes unchecked without a finding.\n\n### Constraints\nEach item keeps the behaviour its origin spec delivered; a fix that changes an answer states it as a decision.\n\n### Non-goals\nReopening the decisions of the origin spec.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: With the POSE root below the repository top, the ready-transition read shall list changed specs (Git names them top-relative), so their ready transitions are checked (round 1 N11, round 5 N3).\n- R2: The report's redaction shall replace a whole absolute path, also one with spaces, quotes, parentheses or a leading `:`, backtick or `[` (round 5, N1).\n- R3: The bounds on Git's message and the report note shall cut at a character, never inside a UTF-8 sequence (round 5, N4).\n- R4: A failing `ls-files` in worktree scope selection shall fail the selection with its cause instead of silently dropping untracked files (round 5, N5).\n- R5: The guards listed by rounds 2–5 shall each have a failing test: restoring `--path-format`, the `X^-` cut, the report note bound and stderr warning, `GitEnglish` on the check, lookup and hand-over, the memfd write fallback, the private copy keeping the index's time, a stand-in Git that echoes an unknown `--path-format`, and a locale test independent of installed translations; the ledger's context is L1 (rounds 1 N6–N7, 2 N16, 3 N21, 5 N2).\n\n### Non-functional\nExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n\n### Security\nNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n\n### Compatibility\nRecords and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n`pose-mcp`: `check.go` (ready transitions), `report.go`, `validate_scope.go`, `git_worktree_reads*.go` and their tests.\n\n### Artifacts\n- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-validate-index-reads-residuals.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_reads_residuals_test.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_index_residuals_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux_test.go\n\n### Delivery targets\n- capability:validate-index-reads-residuals module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\n\n### Accepted limits\n- L1: The review history ledger passing its own deadline to the index lookup has no failing test. Accepted because observing it needs a stand-in Git that outlasts the ledger's 30 s deadline, and the lookup is bounded by its own 30 s otherwise, so a regression changes the bound, not the outcome.\n\n### API/contract changes\n`pose validate` scope selection fails with its cause when the untracked listing fails, where it used to narrow silently. The report note replaces whole known directories before other absolute paths.\n\n### Data/storage changes\nNone.\n\n### Technical risks\nA scope selection that used to pass with a failing `ls-files` now fails; that failure was silent narrowing before.\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Planning\n- [x] Confirm each requirement against the current engine before starting.\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n\n### Validation\n- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Execution log\n- 2026-11-27: R1 adds `--relative` to the ready-transition diff; R2 replaces the root, repository top, Git directories, temporary and home directories whole before the generic pattern, which now also starts after `:`, a backtick or `[`; R3 cuts at a character (`TruncateUTF8`); R4 fails scope selection on a failed untracked listing; R5 adds stand-in Git tests. Each guard fails its test mutated out: `TestReadyTransitionsSeeSpecsBelowTheRepositoryTop`, `TestTheReportRemovesWholePaths`, `TestBoundsCutAtACharacter`, `TestScopeSelectionReportsAFailedUntrackedListing`, `TestTheIndexLookupNeedsNoPathFormat`, `TestIndexReadsRunGitInEnglish`, `TestTheIndexFallbacksKeepTheAnswer`, `TestTheRemainingIndexReadGuards`.\n\n### Results summary\nThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestReadyTransitionsSeeSpecsBelowTheRepositoryTop\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestTheReportRemovesWholePaths\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestBoundsCutAtACharacter\n- R4 [satisfied] test:TestScopeSelectionReportsAFailedUntrackedListing\n- R5 [satisfied] test:TestTheIndexLookupNeedsNoPathFormat, test:TestIndexReadsRunGitInEnglish, test:TestTheIndexFallbacksKeepTheAnswer, test:TestTheRemainingIndexReadGuards\n\n### Known gaps\nNone.\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nReady transitions see specs below the repository top; the report removes whole paths and cuts at characters; a failed untracked listing fails scope selection; every index-read guard but the ledger's deadline has a failing test.\n\n### Files and modules changed\n`pose-mcp` check, report, validate scope and the read-only index reads, with their tests.\n\n### Validation executed\n`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n\n### Residual risks\nL1 above.\n\n### Follow-ups\nNone. Origin: `pose-validate-read-only-index-followups` (done 2026-11-27).\n","numLines":136,"startLine":1,"totalLines":136}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011mUdqaU8specS7yspcCtEC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
