{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChTkMbfKBZidanDdWhPfg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GCGzmSKGqYgGs84m6F2UFD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"printf '%s\\n' 'decision: changes-requested' '```pose-draft' '{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",' '\"findings\":[' '{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\",\"line\":1182,\"summary\":\"R1 is incomplete: with the root below the repository top the new --relative candidates reach `git show HEAD:<root-relative path>`, which Git resolves from the top. The old text comes back empty, so a modified spec already in-progress at HEAD and not ready fails strict check as a new transition (reproduced). A same-named spec at the top would be read instead and could hide a real transition (by reading). The R1 test checks only the candidate list.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":356,\"summary\":\"Regression: replacing known directories as bare substrings leaves the tail of other paths in the versioned report, because the generic pattern no longer matches after <path>. Reproduced with HOME=/home/jane: /home/jane/clients/acme-secret/index gives <path>/clients/acme-secret/index, /home/janet/x gives <path>t/x, and <root>-acme-secret/index gives <path>-acme-secret/index. The base pattern removed these unspaced paths whole.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":356,\"summary\":\"Known directories are also replaced inside relative names: with TMPDIR=/tmp, feature/tmp-cleanup becomes feature<path>-cleanup, and docs/home/jane/notes becomes docs<path>/notes (reproduced). Relative names were kept before.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":364,\"summary\":\"R2 is not met outside the known directories: `open /mnt/jane doe/index` becomes `open <path> doe/index` (reproduced). Spaces, quotes or parentheses still cut the match, while the spec marks R2 satisfied. The test input [/srv/x y] asserts only that /srv is gone, not the tail.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":329,\"summary\":\"By reading, not run on Windows: filepath.Clean turns known directories into backslash form, while Git prints forward slashes, so the whole-directory replacement would not match paths in Git messages there.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N6\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_index_residuals_test.go\",\"line\":60,\"summary\":\"The leading-colon case of R2 has no failing test: with `:` removed from the prefix class, TestTheReportRemovesWholePaths and the other report tests run still pass (mutation by test overlay).\"},' '{\"id\":\"N7\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":105,\"summary\":\"Pre-existing and outside R1-R5: with the root below the repository top, the scope diff lists top-relative paths (no --relative) while ls-files lists root-relative ones. A changed file in a self-contained module is then owned by no module and the module is not selected: changed=[proj/mod/x.txt], selected empty, no error (reproduced). Validation narrows silently.\"}' '],' '\"criteria\":[' '{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\",\"rationale\":\"The assumption that listing the changed specs is enough to check their transitions is false below the repository top. L1 was read and is not disputed.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The change adds no shared mutable state in production; memfdWrite is a test seam restored by its test. Index lookup deadlines are unchanged; L1 covers the ledger one.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N2\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N4\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N2\"},' '{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\",\"rationale\":\"A root below the top that passed check can now fail on a spec that did not transition.\"},' '{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},' '{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N2\",\"rationale\":\"--relative, TruncateUTF8 and the failing untracked listing address their causes. The redaction design (substring replacement before the generic pattern) causes N2 and N3. The design assessment observed no structural deltas.\"},' '{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Examined the spec API/contract section and searched docs-site/docs/cli.md: it states the validate command line but nothing about redaction or listing failure that this change contradicts. The spec states the new selection failure.\"},' '{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The failed untracked listing names the range, the command and the Git message in English, the CLI exits 2 and carry reports the selection as unused. Focused test passed.\"},' '{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N4\"},' '{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The eight code files in the range match the spec artifact list and R1-R5; no unrelated behaviour was added. N7 is outside this scope.\"},' '{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N2\"},' '{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N3\",\"rationale\":\"Replacing known directories is a small design, but without path-boundary handling it is not sufficient: it removes relative text and keeps absolute tails.\"}' '],' '\"tools\":[' '{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-index-reads-residuals --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; it printed orphan-path warnings.\"},' '{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-8c635a2acc70b570\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, no deltas.\"},' '{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},' '{\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Ran with --no-persist.\"},' '{\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"The scan reports itself incomplete: two spec sources could not be read.\"},' '{\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-validate-index-reads-residuals\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; it cannot pass before the review is recorded and the spec is done.\"},' '{\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose review-check spec:pose-validate-index-reads-residuals\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; no review record exists yet.\"},' '{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},' '{\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Ran with --strict: zero findings.\"},' '{\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Rests on the sealed result. The sandbox rerun FAILED: 236 steps, 224 pass, 11 fail, 1 timeout. Seen causes include HTTP 403 and ownership refusals of /var/tmp and /home; runtime-host, delegate-refused, file-mode and timeout failures were not root-caused, and none of the failing test names is one this change adds or edits.\"},' '{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Rests on the sealed result. The sandbox rerun FAILED: 233 steps, 221 pass, 11 fail, 1 error, with network access denied; the eight focused tests of this change passed separately.\"}' ']}' '```' > \"$TMPDIR/draft.md\" && cat \"$TMPDIR/draft.md\" | \"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft - 2>&1 | tail -n 30","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2434,"cache_read_input_tokens":97717,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2434},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"76ced927-735f-424b-aff9-53c25d8884e8","timestamp":"2026-11-27T16:28:52.387Z","request_id":"req_011ChTkMbTfLgqk2kV1WphjV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GCGzmSKGqYgGs84m6F2UFD":{"command":"printf '%s\\n' 'decision: changes-requested' '```pose-draft' '{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",' '\"findings\":[' '{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\",\"line\":1182,\"summary\":\"R1 is incomplete: with the root below the repository 